    <obo:IAO_0000115>An RNA molecule that transfers the coding information for protein synthesis from the chromosomes to the ribosomes mRNA is formed from a DNA template by transcription. It may be a copy of a single gene or of several adjacent genes (polycistronic mRNA). On the ribosome, the sequence is converted into the programmed amino acid sequence through translation.</obo:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:label>mRNA</rdfs:label>
    <craft:annotatable_text>message; messages; messenger RNA; messenger RNAs; mRNA; mRNAs</craft:annotatable_text>
  </owl:Class>
